"following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"assignees":[{"login":"trustin","id":173918,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzkxOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173918?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin","html_url":"https://github.com/trustin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/milestones/29","html_url":"https://github.com/netty/netty/milestone/29","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/milestones/29/labels","id":174364,"node_id":"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lMTc0MzY0","number":29,"title":"4.0.0.Alpha5","description":"","creator":{"login":"normanmaurer","id":439362,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzOTM2Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/439362?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer","html_url":"https://github.com/normanmaurer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":0,"closed_issues":13,"state":"closed","created_at":"2012-09-13T11:48:08Z","updated_at":"2013-09-05T14:15:13Z","due_on":"2012-09-28T07:00:00Z","closed_at":"2012-09-28T08:00:25Z"},"comments":9,"created_at":"2012-09-17T14:44:43Z","updated_at":"2012-09-22T12:57:08Z","closed_at":"2012-09-22T12:57:07Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I've noticed that when using LocalChannels and sending several objects at a time, there would be execptions thrown by the `LocalEventGroup::run()` method. \n\nSpecifically `ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException`.\n\nThe offending method is \n\n``` java\nDefaultChannelHandlerContext.MessageBridge {\n    void fill() {\n            if (msgBuf.isEmpty()) {\n                return;\n            }\n            Object[] data = msgBuf.toArray();  <<<<<<<<<<\n            msgBuf.clear();\n            exchangeBuf.add(data);\n        }\n}\n```\n\nThe relevant method calls are\n\n``` java\n    public Object[] toArray() {\n        return copyElements(new Object[size()]);\n    }\n```\n\n``` java\nprivate <T> T[] copyElements(T[] a) {\n        if (head < tail) {\n            System.arraycopy(elements, head, a, 0, size());\n        } else if (head > tail) {\n            int headPortionLen = elements.length - head;\n            System.arraycopy(elements, head, a, 0, headPortionLen);\n            System.arraycopy(elements, 0, a, headPortionLen, tail);\n        }\n        return a;\n    }\n```\n\nThe specific problem is that the `ArrayDeque` is getting modified between the two calls, as in my case, `a.length=3` and `this.size()=4` in the second method. Since they are different sizes... BLAMMO.\n\nWhat I think might be the issue is something akin to a concurrent modification. Since it's a `ArrayDeque` that is being used, it doesn't throw a `concurrent modification exception`, it just  throws an `exception` when it gets to that point.\n\nI haven't thought exactly how to solve this (maybe some tricks from Brian Goetz will fit the bill). This took a while to track down, and involved connecting/sending messages/disconnecting very, very quickly on local channels.\n\nTo figure out exactly what was going on, I modified `LocalEventLoop` to catch `Exception` in it's run method instead of just `InterruptedException`.\n\n``` java\n        for (;;) {\n            Runnable task;\n            try {\n                task = takeTask();\n                task.run();\n            } catch (Exception e) {  <<<<<<<<<<<<\n                // Waken up by interruptThread()\n                System.err.println(\"WHAT\"); <<<<<<<<<<<\n            }\n\n            if (isShutdown()) {\n                task = pollTask();\n                if (task == null) {\n                    break;\n                }\n                task.run();\n            }\n        }\n```\n\nAs filling the Bridge is used everywhere, I'd imagine this affects everything else. I first noticed it when I started losing messages in my LocalChannel UnitTests.\n","closed_by":{"login":"CodeMason","id":2230263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMzAyNjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2230263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeMason","html_url":"https://github.com/CodeMason","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeMason/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeMason/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeMason/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeMason/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeMason/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeMason/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeMason/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeMason/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeMason/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/issues/608/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/issues/608/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}